course: dictionary
lesson: 10529
title: Tyrants and the power to choose
level: primary-4
stars: 0
explain: A tyrant is a ruler who uses power cruelly and unfairly, and does not let people choose or change their leaders. In a story, a tyrant king might frighten a whole village until a hero stands up to him.
explain: «Mei says the First Emperor was the greatest ruler ever; the teacher says he was a tyrant.» Mei and the teacher disagree about the same ruler. Mei's word, greatest, is praise, so the teacher's word, tyrant, must be a very different kind of judgement.
explain: «He was both a unifier and a tyrant.» The word both is a clue: it tells you two different things are true at once. A unifier brings people together, so a tyrant must be a different kind of ruler, one who rules cruelly and unfairly. Swap in your meaning and check it still makes sense.
fact: Tyrant is a noun: a tyrant, tyrants.
fact: A tyrant is a ruler who uses power cruelly and unfairly.
fact: In an informal sense, a tyrant is anyone who bosses others about cruelly, such as a bossy teacher or older sibling.
fact: In ancient Greece, a tyrant was a ruler who took power by force, and was not always cruel.
fact: Tyranny is the rule of a tyrant, and people fight it with laws, elections and courts.
exercise: What is a tyrant? | A kind teacher who helps everyone | A king loved by all the people | *A ruler who uses power cruelly and unfairly | A scientist who studies birds
exercise: «He was both a unifier and a tyrant.» What does the word both tell you? | That he was a teacher | That he was very tall | *That two different things are true at the same time | That he was chosen by people in an election
exercise: In ancient Greece, a tyrant was a ruler who took power by force. How did a Greek tyrant get power? | By being given it by the children | By asking the people politely | Through a fair election | *By taking it by force
test: In history lessons, a tyrant is the opposite of which kind of leader? | A bossy older sibling | A cruel king who frightens everyone | *A fair leader who was chosen by the people | A giant who lives in a cave
test: Your bossy older sister orders you about cruelly. Which word could describe her, in an informal way? | Emperor | Hero | *Tyrant | Unifier
exam: Dara says a tyrant is a kind helper, but the dictionary says a tyrant is a ruler who uses power cruelly. Which meaning is correct? | A kind helper | A kind bird | *A ruler who uses power cruelly and unfairly | A fair leader chosen by an election
